Treat iOS Reduce Motion as an additional signal; `MediaQuery.disableAnimationsOf(context)` alone only covers the Android case here.

```dart
import 'dart:ui' show PlatformDispatcher;

bool shouldReduceMotion(BuildContext context) {
  final features = PlatformDispatcher.instance.accessibilityFeatures;
  return MediaQuery.disableAnimationsOf(context) || features.reduceMotion;
}
```

Use `shouldReduceMotion(context)` wherever the decorative animation starts or selects its duration. For nonessential motion, immediately show its final/static state (or a minimal fade), rather than playing the full animation.

To react while the screen remains mounted, observe accessibility changes and update state:

```dart
class _DecorativeAnimationState extends State<DecorativeAnimation>
    with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin, WidgetsBindingObserver {
  late final AnimationController _controller;
  bool _reduceMotion = false;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    WidgetsBinding.instance.addObserver(this);
    _controller = AnimationController(
      vsync: this,
      duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 500),
    );
    _syncMotionPreference();
  }

  @override
  void didChangeAccessibilityFeatures() {
    _syncMotionPreference();
  }

  void _syncMotionPreference() {
    final features = PlatformDispatcher.instance.accessibilityFeatures;
    final reduce = features.disableAnimations || features.reduceMotion;

    if (_reduceMotion == reduce) return;
    setState(() => _reduceMotion = reduce);

    if (reduce) {
      _controller.value = 1; // static completed visual
      _controller.stop();
    } else {
      _controller.forward(from: 0);
    }
  }

  @override
  void dispose() {
    WidgetsBinding.instance.removeObserver(this);
    _controller.dispose();
    super.dispose();
  }
}
```

If Android behavior must specifically follow `MediaQuery.disableAnimationsOf`, also recompute that value in `didChangeDependencies()` and combine it with `reduceMotion`.

Verify:

- iOS: enable Reduce Motion with screen reader off; decorative motion must stop even though `MediaQuery.disableAnimationsOf` is false.
- Android: enable Remove animations; existing reduced-motion behavior remains intact.
- Change either setting while the screen is open; the animation stops or resumes without leaving/reopening the route.
- Check initial, active, completed, and interrupted states, and confirm the controller is disposed with the screen.
